    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0198" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg876"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Clay.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    reception of your two despatches, namely: No. 16, of the 25th of July, and No.
                    17, of the 5th of August.</p>
                <p>The information recently received from Europe confirms the impression I have
                    already communicated to you, that the western powers will take care to avoid a
                    war with Russia, at least throughout the present year.</p>
                <p>Your suggestions in regard to the policy proper to be observed in reference to
                    the conduct of our civil war, and the subject of slavery, has been submitted to
                    the President.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius</hi> M. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Clay</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
